# Floats have their copies behind the front of a loop where the loop's own text multiplies or divides an element of the holder. The text was read from the element on, along its ONLY user: an element with two users,
# one of them a product, counted as multiplied by nobody, and a variance over a Float64Array went by the copy of all views: 27.9 > 53.3 instructions an element.
# Each product of the loop is asked for its factors instead.
# f1 = go
